      "id": 1,
      "text": "In the late 1960s, Downer Road was renamed Blossom Hill to link it with the stretch coming from Los Gatos.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.metrosiliconvalley.com/hill-of-a-stretch/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The earliest segment of Blossom Hill Road dates back to the 1920s, originally running only through Los Gatos.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.metrosiliconvalley.com/hill-of-a-stretch/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "From the Gatos hills, drivers can still see sweeping valley rooftops, a view that once showed only orchards and blossoms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.metrosiliconvalley.com/hill-of-a-stretch/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After crossing Interstate 101, Blossom Hill Road transforms into Silver Creek Valley Road, a change that occurred within the last quarter century.",
